-- title:
--   Unnumbered (44)–(45): pure-state operator coefficients and support lower bound
-- statement:
--   All Hilbert spaces have positive finite dimension. Channels are completely positive and trace preserving; conjugates use the same normalized pure-environment dilation. Let $T=(T_m)$ be a basis of $d^2$ unitaries on $\mathbb C^d$, including $I$, with $\operatorname{Tr}(T_m^\dagger T_n)=d\delta_{mn}$. For a density matrix $\rho$ define $v_m=\operatorname{Tr}(T_m^\dagger\rho)$, with $0$ the identity label. Then
--
--   $$
--   \rho=\frac1d\sum_m v_mT_m,\qquad v_0=1,\qquad |v_m|\le1.
--   $$
--
--   For pure $\rho$, $\sum_{m\ne0}|v_m|^2=d-1$, so at least $d$ coefficients are nonzero. Every finite set containing their support, and any subgroup generated by it when a label group is given, has at least $d$ elements. The printed intermediate factor $d^{-2}$ is corrected to $d^{-1}$.
-- source:
--   Properties of Conjugate Channels with Applications to Additivity and Multiplicativity, arXiv:quant-ph/0509126v3, PDF p. 17, Unnumbered (44)–(45): pure-state operator coefficients and support lower bound

